# Concise product UI

This app is a dense Jira workspace (daily board, roadmap, settings, etc.). Prefer clarity over explanation. Do not write marketing or tutorial prose into the UI.

## Copy density

- One job per section: title + at most one short supporting line.
- Page `subtitle` / hero lines: max ~12 words (EN) / ~15 words (FA).
- Helper text under fields: one line. Prefer a good `placeholder` over a paragraph.
- Empty states: title ≤ 6 words; hint ≤ 1 sentence. No setup essays.
- Buttons/labels: verb + object (`Log work`, `ثبت کار`) — no filler.
- Toast / success / error: one short sentence. Point to the fix, don’t narrate the system.
- EN and FA strings stay parallel and equally short — don’t inflate one language.

## Layout clutter

- Don’t stack cards, banners, and long descriptions that repeat the same idea.
- Prefer whitespace and hierarchy over extra borders, nested panels, or decorative chrome.
- Put deep how-to in docs/tooltips only when the control is genuinely unclear — not by default.
- Filters and primary actions stay scannable; don’t bury them under instructional blocks.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
subtitle: "Check active tickets for the current project, log time spent, or use AI to parse your daily summary and log work in batch."
aiBoxDesc: "Enter your daily accomplishments in plain text (English or Persian). The AI will identify matching tickets, distribute your hours, and write professional worklog descriptions."

// ✅ GOOD
subtitle: "Active tickets, quick log, or AI batch log."
aiBoxDesc: "Paste today’s work; AI matches tickets and hours."
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — empty state essay
emptyHint: "Please connect to your self-hosted Jira Server first in '1. Connection & Config' tab to view your daily board."

// ✅ GOOD
emptyHint: "Connect Jira in Settings, then refresh."
```

When adding or rewriting UI strings, shorten first; only expand if the user cannot complete the task without the extra words.
